course: dictionary
lesson: 1569
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. The word charcoal can mean a black fuel, a stick for drawing, or a very dark grey colour. The words around it tell you which meaning is right. «Smelting heats ore with fuel such as charcoal or coke to free the metal.» Here charcoal is a fuel, because the ore is heated to free the metal.
explain: Ask yourself what the sentence is about. If it is about barbecues, fire or heating, charcoal is the black material. If it is about drawing, lines or smudges, it is the stick. If it is about clothes or colours, it is the grey. Then put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Some words also tell you about science. Wood heated slowly with very little air turns into charcoal. «Wood gives off gases that burn with flames; charcoal has already had its gases driven off, so it glows instead.» The clue is in the word already: the gases have gone, so the charcoal glows rather than flames.
fact: Charcoal is a black material made by burning wood slowly with very little air.
fact: A charcoal is a stick of charcoal used for drawing, or a drawing made with it.
fact: Charcoal grey is a very dark grey colour.
fact: «Burning charcoal gives off carbon monoxide, an invisible poisonous gas, so barbecues must never be brought indoors or into a tent.»
fact: Hot charcoal stays hot for hours, so never touch it, even when it looks grey and cold.
exercise: In «Smelting heats ore with fuel such as charcoal or coke to free the metal», what is charcoal? | A stick used for drawing | *A fuel used to heat ore | A very dark grey colour
exercise: An artist says, «I drew the bowl with charcoal, then smudged the lines with my thumb.» What is the charcoal here? | A very dark grey colour | A kind of paint for walls | *A stick used for drawing | A black fuel for barbecues
exercise: Find the word that means a very dark grey colour: «She wore a charcoal coat to the wedding.» | *charcoal | coat | wore | wedding
test: Why must barbecues never be brought into a tent? | Charcoal is too heavy to carry | The tent would be too dark to see inside | *Burning charcoal gives off carbon monoxide, a deadly gas
test: In «people painted horses, bulls and deer with colours made from earth and charcoal», what is charcoal used for? | *Making colours for cave paintings | Making a grey coat for the painter | Cooking the meat of the animals | Lighting the cave at night
exam: In «Smelting heats ore with fuel such as charcoal or coke (a fuel made from coal) to free the metal», which clue tells you what coke is? | smelting | *a fuel made from coal | ore | free the metal
